lemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609  \\n\\n**Author**: Yiling-J  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-01-13T13:45:43Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-13T01:26:12Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/gin_multipartform` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +95 / -0 across 3 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Review Comments (28)\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/test/gintrace_test.go` — 2025-01-13T14:56:36Z\\n\\nI believe the content of `ff` can be detected here.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/test/gintrace_test.go` — 2025-01-13T14:59:10Z\\n\\nassert.NoError?\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 117) — 2025-01-13T15:02:32Z\\n\\nI'm wondering, if there's another middleware layer outside this one, would it be removed because of this?\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/test/gintrace_test.go` — 2025-01-13T15:27:41Z\\n\\nThe goal of the test is to ensure that temporary files are automatically removed, not to test multipart file parsing. The sole purpose of using `c.FormFile` is to trigger multipart parsing, which creates temporary files. I added a `fileHeader.Open()` test in this function to confirm that the temporary file is available. However, I think checking the value of `ff` is unnecessary.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"flc1125 comment 2025 11 11t13 20 30z flc1125 comment 2025 11 11t13 59 33z akats7 comment 2025 11 11t15 42 57z yile j comment 2025 11 12t01 28 14z akats7 comment 2025 11 12t10 24 52z sourc id src pr 01 pull request fix otelgin remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 author yile j creat 2025 01 13t13 45 43z updat 2025 11 13t01 26 12z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open branch fix gin _ multipartform main chang 95 0 across 3 file label mileston review comment 28 flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin test gintrac _ test go 2025 01 13t14 56 36z i believ the content of ff can be detect here flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin test gintrac _ test go 2025 01 13t14 59 10z assert noerror flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 117 2025 01 13t15 02 32z i m wonder if there s anoth middlewar layer outsid this one would it be remov becaus of this yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin test gintrac _ test go 2025 01 13t15 27 41z the goal of the test is to ensur that temporari file are automat remov not to test multipart file pars the sole purpos of use c formfil is to trigger multipart pars which creat temporari file i ad a filehead open test in this function to confirm that the temporari file is avail howev i think check the valu of ff is unnecessari\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"05841978e5499c27\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3030517739595699, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11680614851367127, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7376249, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"We should also decide whether to fix this in otelgin only, or to review other middlewares and address the issue there as well if it exists.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-11-04T00:35:28Z\\n\\n> let’s reach an agreement on how we should fix it\\n\\nWe tend to only need to add the following on the basis of the original main branch:\\n\\n```go\\n\\nc.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()\\n\\n```\\n\\n> We should also decide whether to fix this in otelgin only, or to review other middlewares and address the issue there as well if it exists.\\n\\nIn fact, all middleware based on `*http.Request` has issues whenever a situation like `c.Request.WithContext(c.Request.Context())` occurs, so other components also need to be fixed.\\n\\nHowever, for this current PR, we only need to fix otelgin to keep the PR as minimal as possible. For other middleware, if you are interested, you can also submit fixes in the form of minimal PRs for individual components.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-11-04T01:19:00Z\\n\\n@flc1125 `RemoveAll()` works for me. I think my original PR already aligns well with the goal, it looks like I just need to resolve the conflicts and make sure the tests pass. Let me confirm agin that we’re all in agreement on this approach. @dmathieu @akats7\\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-11-10T01:45:42Z\\n\\nSorry just got caught up on this thread. My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data. \\n\\nWhat about making it configurable with an Option, with the default behavior being to clean it up. That way the user can have more control over which middleware cleans up the form data.\\n\\nI don't want to stall this issue further but just a thought.\\n\\ncc. @flc1125 @dmathieu  \\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-11-10T01:53:34Z\\n\\n> Sorry just got caught up on this thread. My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data.\\n\\nAgree.\\n\\n> What about making it configurable with an Option, with the default behavior being to clean it up. That way the user can have more control over which middleware cleans up the form data.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"we should also decid whether to fix this in otelgin onli or to review other middlewar and address the issu there a well if it exist flc1125 2025 11 04t00 35 28z let s reach an agreement on how we should fix it we tend to onli need to add the follow on the basi of the origin main branch go c request multipartform removeal we should also decid whether to fix this in otelgin onli or to review other middlewar and address the issu there a well if it exist in fact all middlewar base on http request ha issu whenev a situat like c request withcontext c request context occur so other compon also need to be fix howev for this current pr we onli need to fix otelgin to keep the pr a minim a possibl for other middlewar if you are interest you can also submit fix in the form of minim pr for individu compon yile j 2025 11 04t01 19 00z flc1125 removeal work for me i think my origin pr alreadi align well with the goal it look like i just need to resolv the conflict and make sure the test pas let me confirm agin that we re all in agreement on this approach dmathieu akats7 akats7 2025 11 10t01 45 42z sorri just got caught up on this thread my onli concern with removeal is on the off chanc that a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data what about make it configur with an option with the default behavior be to clean it up that way the user can have more control over which middlewar clean up the form data i don t want to stall this issu further but just a thought cc flc1125 dmathieu flc1125 2025 11 10t01 53 34z sorri just got caught up on this thread my onli concern with removeal is on the off chanc that a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data agre what about make it configur with an option with the default behavior be to clean it up that way the user can have more control over which middlewar clean up the form data\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"3c8bf7e7b452e3f2\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29982548395956987, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11680614851367127, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7268706, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I would lean towards the solution proposed by the SIG: only support configurability when users explicitly request it. After all, enabling configurability after `RemoveAll()` is an operation that ensures both extensibility compatibility and backward compatibility.\\n\\n@akats7 @dmathieu \\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-11-10T02:01:52Z\\n\\nAh gotcha, didn't see that that was mentioned. I'm good on holding off until it's explicitly requested.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-11-10T04:27:26Z\\n\\n@Yiling-J I think we're good to resolve the conflicts and close this out, thanks!\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-11-10T11:58:48Z\\n\\nI’ve resolved the conflicts, and the otelgin package tests passed on my machine @flc1125 @dmathieu @akats7 \\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-11-10T14:02:53Z\\n\\nCould you add the corresponding unit tests for this scenario?\\n\\n> My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-11-10T15:21:14Z\\n\\n> Could you add the corresponding unit tests for this scenario?\\n\\n> \\n\\n> > My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data.\\n\\nI’ve added more details to the test case, it now includes two extra middlewares, one upstream and one downstream, to demonstrate what happens when `RemoveAll` is called in the otel middleware. The behavior is correct to me, but let’s confirm that we all agree it’s the expected one.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609  \\n\\n**Author**: Yiling-J  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-01-13T13:45:43Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-13T01:26:12Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/gin_multipartform` → `main`  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i would lean toward the solut propos by the sig onli support configur when user explicit request it after all enabl configur after removeal is an oper that ensur both extens compat and backward compat akats7 dmathieu akats7 2025 11 10t02 01 52z ah gotcha didn t see that that wa mention i m good on hold off until it s explicit request akats7 2025 11 10t04 27 26z yile j i think we re good to resolv the conflict and close this out thank yile j 2025 11 10t11 58 48z i ve resolv the conflict and the otelgin packag test pass on my machin flc1125 dmathieu akats7 flc1125 2025 11 10t14 02 53z could you add the correspond unit test for this scenario my onli concern with removeal is on the off chanc that a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data yile j 2025 11 10t15 21 14z could you add the correspond unit test for this scenario my onli concern with removeal is on the off chanc that a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data i ve ad more detail to the test case it now includ two extra middlewar one upstream and one downstream to demonstr what happen when removeal is call in the otel middlewar the behavior is correct to me but let s confirm that we all agre it s the expect one sourc id src pr 01 pull request fix otelgin remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 author yile j creat 2025 01 13t13 45 43z updat 2025 11 13t01 26 12z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open branch fix gin _ multipartform main\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"8a1254612e6e6337\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2978090449824402, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10184799283205749, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7550515, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"me