dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"=== RUN   TestIssue_Middleware\\n\\n    issue_test.go:55: req0.0: 0x140001b6500, req.URL: 0x14000130360\\n\\n    issue_test.go:15: req1.0: 0x140001b6500, req.URL: 0x14000130360\\n\\n    issue_test.go:20: req2.0: 0x140001b6500, req.URL: 0x14000130360\\n\\n    issue_test.go:30: req2.1: 0x140001b6640, req.URL: 0x14000130360\\n\\n    issue_test.go:34: req2.2: 0x140001b6640, req.URL: 0x140001303f0\\n\\n    issue_test.go:24: req2.3: 0x140001b6640, req.URL: 0x140001303f0\\n\\n    issue_test.go:26: req2.4: 0x140001b6780, req.URL: 0x140001303f0\\n\\n    issue_test.go:43: req3.0: 0x140001b6640, req.URL: 0x140001303f0\\n\\n    issue_test.go:44: req3.1: value\\n\\n--- PASS: TestIssue_Middleware (0.00s)\\n\\nPASS\\n\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-01-14T15:29:23Z\\n\\nI skipped the failed test on the Windows platform. This is consistent with how Go handles form cleanup tests (https://github.com/golang/go/blob/6da16013ba4444e0d71540f68279f0283a92d05d/src/net/http/serve_test.go#L7028), so I think it’s fine.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-11-03T13:01:49Z\\n\\n@Yiling-J Hi, are you still willing to handle this issue?\\n\\nAccording to the SIG discussion, it is recommended that middleware remove temporary resources.\\n\\ncc @akats7 \\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-11-03T15:41:21Z\\n\\n> are you still willing to handle this issue\\n\\n@flc1125 Yes. But first, let’s reach an agreement on how we should fix it. As I proposed a while ago, I prefer the reattach approach: “copy the cloned `Request.MultipartForm` value back to the original request before returning,” as mentioned in https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455#issuecomment-3099652232.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"run testissu _ middlewar issu _ test go 55 req0 0 0x140001b6500 req url 0x14000130360 issu _ test go 15 req1 0 0x140001b6500 req url 0x14000130360 issu _ test go 20 req2 0 0x140001b6500 req url 0x14000130360 issu _ test go 30 req2 1 0x140001b6640 req url 0x14000130360 issu _ test go 34 req2 2 0x140001b6640 req url 0x140001303f0 issu _ test go 24 req2 3 0x140001b6640 req url 0x140001303f0 issu _ test go 26 req2 4 0x140001b6780 req url 0x140001303f0 issu _ test go 43 req3 0 0x140001b6640 req url 0x140001303f0 issu _ test go 44 req3 1 valu pas testissu _ middlewar 0 00s pas yile j 2025 01 14t15 29 23z i skip the fail test on the window platform this is consist with how go handl form cleanup test http github com golang go blob 6da16013ba4444e0d71540f68279f0283a92d05d src net http serv _ test go l7028 so i think it s fine flc1125 2025 11 03t13 01 49z yile j hi are you still will to handl this issu accord to the sig discuss it is recommend that middlewar remov temporari resourc cc akats7 yile j 2025 11 03t15 41 21z are you still will to handl this issu flc1125 yes but first let s reach an agreement on how we should fix it a i propos a while ago i prefer the reattach approach copi the clone request multipartform valu back to the origin request befor return a mention in http github com golang go issu 74455 issuecom 3099652232\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"168d6f7543eb6616\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29327985498244025, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10184799283205749, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7399542, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I think this approach could work, but it feels a bit unusual to enforce form parsing in the middleware.\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T16:18:27Z\\n\\nHaving to force remove multipart files is a bit unusual too.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:44:13Z\\n\\nI'm probably more in favor of doing the initialization on the original request as well, explicitly handling clean up logic does seem a bit strange\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:49:47Z\\n\\n@dmathieu maybe we should discuss this in the SIG since it might have implications in the other instrumentation modules\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:50:46Z\\n\\nI won't be able to attend this week's meeting (it's the week where it's late for EU). But yes, feel free to bring it there.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-19T18:17:34Z\\n\\n@Yiling-J what are you thoughts on parsing the form in the middleware, the more I think about it, the more that seems to be the better approach, for example what about certain edge cases where down the chain middlewares might want to access the files\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-20T01:52:04Z\\n\\n@akats7 Another option is to save `c.Request` to a variable before calling `c.Request.WithContext(ctx)`. Then, in the defer function, if `c.Request.MultipartForm != nil`, we can reattach the `MultipartForm` to the original request. This way, there won’t be any automatic removing or parsing. If other middlewares handle the form correctly, this approach should work. \\n\\nIn [http/server.go](https://github.com/golang/go/blob/40b3c0e58a0ae8dec4684a009bf3806769e0fc41/src/net/http/server.go#L2102), the `ServeHTTP` method is called first, which invokes the Gin handlers/middlewares, and then `finishRequest` is called, which removes the temporary files.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i think this approach could work but it feel a bit unusu to enforc form pars in the middlewar dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t16 18 27z have to forc remov multipart file is a bit unusu too akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 44 13z i m probabl more in favor of do the initi on the origin request a well explicit handl clean up logic doe seem a bit strang akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 49 47z dmathieu mayb we should discus this in the sig sinc it might have implic in the other instrument modul dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 50 46z i won t be abl to attend this week s meet it s the week where it s late for eu but yes feel free to bring it there akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 19t18 17 34z yile j what are you thought on pars the form in the middlewar the more i think about it the more that seem to be the better approach for exampl what about certain edg case where down the chain middlewar might want to access the file yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 20t01 52 04z akats7 anoth option is to save c request to a variabl befor call c request withcontext ctx then in the defer function if c request multipartform nil we can reattach the multipartform to the origin request this way there won t be ani automat remov or pars if other middlewar handl the form correct this approach should work in http server go http github com golang go blob 40b3c0e58a0ae8dec4684a009bf3806769e0fc41 src net http server go l2102 the servehttp method is call first which invok the gin handler middlewar and then finishrequest is call which remov the temporari file\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"b3dbc649c958ce01\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29324890763385997, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11182009661980001, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7165828, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"```\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T08:21:31Z\\n\\nWouldn't we be fixing this rather more easily with the following:\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n\\t\\tc.Request = c.Request.Clone(ctx)\\n\\n```\\n\\n[WithContext](https://pkg.go.dev/net/http#Request.WithContext) performs a shallow clone, and therefore doesn't clone the multipart form.\\n\\nHowever, [Clone](https://pkg.go.dev/net/http#Request.Clone) performs a deep copy, and makes an explicit clone of [MultipartForm](https://cs.opensource.google/go/go/+/refs/tags/go1.23.4:src/net/http/request.go;l=406).\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T14:39:53Z\\n\\nThe problem here is, go http request will call MultipartForm.RemoveAll() automatically when request finishes. However, the otelgin middleware creates a new request, and temporary files will be stored in this new request's MultipartForm field. Unfortunately, no one is calling MultipartForm.RemoveAll() on this new request.\\n\\nA deep clone wouldn’t resolve the problem because the MultipartForm is also copied. A shallow clone might seem like it should work since the MultipartForm field is shared, but it doesn’t. This is because the MultipartForm field is lazily initialized—it’s only assigned a value when you [parse the form](https://github.com/golang/go/blob/6da16013ba4444e0d71540f68279f0283a92d05d/src/net/http/request.go#L1403). As a result, in the middleware, the field is nil.\\n\\nRelated issues: https://github.com/golang/go/issues/58809, https://github.com/labstack/echo/issues/2413\\n\\nI think other OpenTelemetry middlewares, such as otelmux and otelehco, might also have the same issue.\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T14:55:45Z\\n\\nWhat if we parse the form before making the new request?\\n\\nWouldn't we share the object then?\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T15:31:10Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t08 21 31z wouldn t we be fix this rather more easili with the follow suggest c request c request clone ctx withcontext http pkg go dev net http request withcontext perform a shallow clone and therefor doesn t clone the multipart form howev clone http pkg go dev net http request clone perform a deep copi and make an explicit clone of multipartform http c opensourc googl go go ref tag go1 23 4 src net http request go l 406 yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t14 39 53z the problem here is go http request will call multipartform removeal automat when request finish howev the otelgin middlewar creat a new request and temporari file will be store in this new request s multipartform field unfortun no one is call multipartform removeal on this new request a deep clone wouldn t resolv the problem becaus the multipartform is also copi a shallow clone might seem like it should work sinc the multipartform field is share but it doesn t this is becaus the multipartform field is lazili initi it s onli assign a valu when you pars the form http github com golang go blob 6da16013ba4444e0d71540f68279f0283a92d05d src net http request go l1403 a a result in the middlewar the field is nil relat issu http github com golang go issu 58809 http github com labstack echo issu 2413 i think other opentelemetri middlewar such a otelmux and otelehco might also have the same issu dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t14 55 45z what if we pars the form befor make the new request wouldn t we share the object then yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t15 31 10z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"0b66ff59ca7469a0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2857350649824402, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10184799283205749, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7148049, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"Pull request 6609 latest November 2025 review disposition merge blockers temporary MultipartForm RemoveAll reattach prototype 8161\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
