{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"question":"issue 5946 July 2025 marked duplicate dmathieu duplicate of what related issue 4588 status"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"However, this approach will also introduce additional side effects, for which there is currently no better solution.  \\n\\n**Impact:**  \\n\\nAssuming our middleware is wrapped in the following manner: `m1(m2(otel-middleware(m3(fn))))`,  \\n\\nwhere `m1` and `m2` internally implement operations such as `request.ParseMultipartForm(1)`. Due to the effect of `RemoveAll` in `otel-middleware`,  \\n\\nthere may be cases where they repeatedly create `request.MultipartForm` resources, resulting in additional memory allocations.\\n\\nOf course, we can also choose not to handle it, but we need to remind users to process `c.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()`.\\n\\n----\\n\\nI'd like to hear your opinions: @akats7 @open-telemetry/go-approvers \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-01]\\n\\n# Issue: Using otelgin.Middleware will cause temporary MultipartForm files not to be destroyed. (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#5946)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946  \\n\\n**Author**: zacklpx  \\n\\n**Created**: 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **Updated**: 2025-07-03T13:28:05Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelgin  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Timeline\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `area: instrumentation`\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `bug`\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `instrumentation: otelgin`\\n\\n- 2024-11-21T12:21:58Z · **cross-referenced** by flc1125 ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/4588\\n\\n- 2025-01-13T13:45:45Z · **cross-referenced** by Yiling-J ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609\\n\\n- 2025-07-02T08:06:05Z · **marked_as_duplicate** by dmathieu\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"howev this approach will also introduc addit side effect for which there is current no better solut impact assum our middlewar is wrap in the follow manner m1 m2 otel middlewar m3 fn where m1 and m2 intern implement oper such a request parsemultipartform 1 due to the effect of removeal in otel middlewar there may be case where they repeat creat request multipartform resourc result in addit memori alloc of cours we can also choos not to handl it but we need to remind user to process c request multipartform removeal i d like to hear your opinion akats7 open telemetri go approv sourc id src issu 01 issu use otelgin middlewar will caus temporari multipartform file not to be destroy open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 5946 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 author zacklpx creat 2024 07 25t03 50 39z updat 2025 07 03t13 28 05z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open label bug area instrument instrument otelgin mileston timelin 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx area instrument 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx bug 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx instrument otelgin 2024 11 21t12 21 58z cross referenc by flc1125 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 4588 2025 01 13t13 45 45z cross referenc by yile j http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 2025 07 02t08 06 05z mark _ a _ duplic by dmathieu\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"id\": \"5b39be36d40588b5\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.36365934779634795, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2179850854233542, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70356596, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 16121, \"chunk_count\": 10, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 5002, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I also disagree that folks should do this themselves. Especially since this has been the default behavior for many years now (and the same behavior exists for other instrumentations, such as otelecho).\\n\\nI think this discussion would be better synchronously though. If you're able to, I'd recommend you to join our next SIG meeting (tomorrow at 4pm UTC).\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/community/?tab=readme-ov-file#implementation-sigs\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T08:48:08Z\\n\\n> I disagree with this being a violation of Go's conventions (in the context of the middleware pattern, we don't flow forward. At the end of a middleware, we go back to its parent). I also disagree that folks should do this themselves. Especially since this has been the default behavior for many years now (and the same behavior exists for other instrumentations, such as otelecho).\\n\\n> \\n\\n> I think this discussion would be better synchronously though. If you're able to, I'd recommend you to join our next SIG meeting (tomorrow at 4pm UTC). https://github.com/open-telemetry/community/?tab=readme-ov-file#implementation-sigs\\n\\nOk well one thing is for certain, you all have a much better understanding of the existing patterns and user expectations for this project than I do. It's getting quite late for me so I'll sleep on this and give your points their time to marinate. As far as the SIG meeting goes that's a great idea (and sounds fun too) - unfortunately that's a fairly busy time for me but I'll do my best to make it.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T08:59:49Z\\n\\n> Especially since this has been the default behavior for many years now (and the same behavior exists for other instrumentations, such as otelecho).\\n\\nThis is a strong argument, I didn’t realize that was the case.  I wasn’t looking to add a breaking change and I’m glad you pointed it out. I’ll see what I can do to come up with something that maintains the existing semantics while also fixing the race.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-10-17T10:41:58Z\\n\\nWe have been discussing this in yesterday's SIG meeting, and have decided this fix is incorrect and the current behavior is the proper one.\\n\\nSee https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/4588#issuecomment-3414917592\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i also disagre that folk should do this themselv especi sinc this ha been the default behavior for mani year now and the same behavior exist for other instrument such a otelecho i think this discuss would be better synchron though if you re abl to i d recommend you to join our next sig meet tomorrow at 4pm utc http github com open telemetri communiti tab readm ov file implement sig nicksherron 2025 10 14t08 48 08z i disagre with this be a violat of go s convent in the context of the middlewar pattern we don t flow forward at the end of a middlewar we go back to it parent i also disagre that folk should do this themselv especi sinc this ha been the default behavior for mani year now and the same behavior exist for other instrument such a otelecho i think this discuss would be better synchron though if you re abl to i d recommend you to join our next sig meet tomorrow at 4pm utc http github com open telemetri communiti tab readm ov file implement sig ok well one thing is for certain you all have a much better understand of the exist pattern and user expect for this project than i do it s get quit late for me so i ll sleep on this and give your point their time to marin a far a the sig meet go that s a great idea and sound fun too unfortun that s a fair busi time for me but i ll do my best to make it nicksherron 2025 10 14t08 59 49z especi sinc this ha been the default behavior for mani year now and the same behavior exist for other instrument such a otelecho this is a strong argument i didn t realiz that wa the case i wasn t look to add a break chang and i m glad you point it out i ll see what i can do to come up with someth that maintain the exist semant while also fix the race dmathieu 2025 10 17t10 41 58z we have been discuss this in yesterday s sig meet and have decid this fix is incorrect and the current behavior is the proper one see http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 4588 issuecom 3414917592\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"b87d58f69aed9a06\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3140035467914152, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17250003827345026, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6441784, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  ctx := cfg.Propagators.Extract(savedCtx, ...)\\n\\n  // After: Use context directly (correct)\\n\\n  reqCtx := c.Request.Context()\\n\\n  ctx := cfg.Propagators.Extract(reqCtx, ...)\\n\\n```\\n\\n  The behavior is identical except:\\n\\n  -  No race condition\\n\\n  -  Better performance\\n\\n  -  Simpler code\\n\\n  -  Tests pass with -race\\n\\n  Conclusion\\n\\n  This is a straightforward bug fix that:\\n\\n  1. Removes unnecessary code that causes a race\\n\\n  2. Improves performance (fewer allocations, no defer overhead)\\n\\n  3. Fixes a 2-year-old issue (#4588)\\n\\n  4. Follows precedent from previous race fixes in this project\\n\\n  5. Enables CI to enforce race-free code\\n\\n  There is no downside to this change, and significant benefits. I respectfully request approval to merge.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-10-14T04:58:07Z\\n\\nHi @nicksherron, \\n\\nIt's a fair question, I also don't really see the benefit of it, I'm going to assume it was added for hygiene to avoid leaking the modifications out of the intended request's middleware chain.\\n\\n@flc1125 what are your thoughts, even if it doesn't provide thread safety it does seem valid\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-10-14T05:01:16Z\\n\\n> I'm going to assume it was added for hygiene to avoid leaking the modifications out of the intended request's middleware chain.\\n\\nI agree with this situation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T05:06:09Z\\n\\nI'm confused about this \\\"doesn't provide thread safety\\\" claim. I'm starring at a test failure due to data race when running `go test -race`  in one of my projects that clearly points the finger to the code I removed as being the culprit. When I do a `go mod -replace` using my change in this PR the race goes away. \\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-10-14T05:09:52Z\\n\\n> I'm confused about this \\\"doesn't provide thread safety\\\" claim. I'm starring at a test failure due to data race when running `go test -race` in one of my projects that clearly points the finger to the code I removed as being the culprit. When I do a `go mod -replace` using my change in this PR the race goes away.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"ctx cfg propag extract savedctx after use context direct correct reqctx c request context ctx cfg propag extract reqctx the behavior is ident except no race condit better perform simpler code test pas with race conclus this is a straightforward bug fix that 1 remov unnecessari code that caus a race 2 improv perform fewer alloc no defer overhead 3 fix a2 year old issu 4588 4 follow preced from previous race fix in this project 5 enabl ci to enforc race free code there is no downsid to this chang and signific benefit i respect request approv to merg akats7 2025 10 14t04 58 07z hi nicksherron it s a fair question i also don t realli see the benefit of it i m go to assum it wa ad for hygien to avoid leak the modif out of the intend request s middlewar chain flc1125 what are your thought even if it doesn t provid thread safeti it doe seem valid flc1125 2025 10 14t05 01 16z i m go to assum it wa ad for hygien to avoid leak the modif out of the intend request s middlewar chain i agre with this situat nicksherron 2025 10 14t05 06 09z i m confus about this doesn t provid thread safeti claim i m star at a test failur due to data race when run go test race in one of my project that clear point the finger to the code i remov a be the culprit when i do a go mod replac use my chang in this pr the race go away flc1125 2025 10 14t05 09 52z i m confus about this doesn t provid thread safeti claim i m star at a test failur due to data race when run go test race in one of my project that clear point the finger to the code i remov a be the culprit when i do a go mod replac use my chang in this pr the race go away\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"cad80d2ecd6e532f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31028982879141515, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17250003827345023, \"vector_similarity\": 0.63179934, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  These fixes were accepted because data races are bugs, not \\\"concurrency mechanisms left to users.\\\"\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Race Is Real and Reproducible\\n\\n  From issue #4588:\\n\\n  WARNING: DATA RACE\\n\\n  Write at 0x... by goroutine X:\\n\\n    [defer in Middleware]\\n\\n  Read at 0x... by goroutine Y:\\n\\n    [user handler accessing context]\\n\\n  This is undefined behavior. The Go memory model states: \\\"Programs that modify data being simultaneously accessed by multiple goroutines must serialize such access.\\\"\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Fix is Correct\\n\\n  The fix simply removes dead code:\\n\\n```go\\n\\n  // Before: Save and restore (unnecessary)\\n\\n  savedCtx := c.Request.Context()\\n\\n  defer func() { c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(savedCtx) }()\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"these fix were accept becaus data race are bug not concurr mechan left to user sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston the race is real and reproduc from issu 4588 warn data race write at 0x by goroutin x defer in middlewar read at 0x by goroutin y user handler access context this is undefin behavior the go memori model state program that modifi data be simultan access by multipl goroutin must serial such access sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston the fix is correct the fix simpli remov dead code go befor save and restor unnecessari savedctx c request context defer func c request c request withcontext savedctx\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"b40b58fd0d2fea42\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3051376729310379, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15827118704433984, \"vector_similarity\": 0.64782614, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-04]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479584781  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:18:08Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:18:08Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-16\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n*   Tyler Yahn\\n\\n*   Damien Mathieu\\n\\n*   Bryan Boreham\\n\\n*   David Ashpole\\n\\n*   Robert Pająk\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**1. otelgin Context Reversal in DataRace**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** raised an issue regarding context reversal in DataRace for otelgin. The context, stored within the otelgin struct, is reverted after middleware execution to prevent parent middlewares from accessing the span. However, Go routines spawned after a request might still need the span in their context. This discussion was based on [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014).\\n\\n*   Damien believes the current behavior is correct and that users should explicitly pass the current context to spawned Go routines. He cited the collector's pattern of passing context directly outside HTTP requests for processors and exporters as a good example.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn** agreed, suggesting that passing necessary values like the span to spawned Go routines is the appropriate solution. He also mentioned OpenTelemetry's pattern of linking spans for asynchronous operations rather than making them child references.\\n\\n**2. otelgin Middleware and Temporary Multi-part Forms**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** brought up an issue where using middleware causes temporary multi-part forms not to be destroyed. This occurs because the instrumentation clones the HTTP request, but the multipart form is not duplicated, preventing proper cleanup. This issue is a historical one, manifesting in otelgin but potentially affecting virtually all HTTP-related middleware.\\n\\n*   References for this issue include:\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946)\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 04 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479584781 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 18 08z updat 2025 11 03t09 18 08z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 16 attende tyler yahn damien mathieu bryan boreham david ashpol robert paj ą k transcript 1 otelgin context revers in datarac damien mathieu rais an issu regard context revers in datarac for otelgin the context store within the otelgin struct is revert after middlewar execut to prevent parent middlewar from access the span howev go routin spawn after a request might still need the span in their context this discuss wa base on http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 damien belief the current behavior is correct and that user should explicit pas the current context to spawn go routin he cite the collector s pattern of pass context direct outsid http request for processor and export a a good exampl tyler yahn agre suggest that pass necessari valu like the span to spawn go routin is the appropri solut he also mention opentelemetri s pattern of link span for asynchron oper rather than make them child refer 2 otelgin middlewar and temporari multi part form damien mathieu brought up an issu where use middlewar caus temporari multi part form not to be destroy this occur becaus the instrument clone the http request but the multipart form is not duplic prevent proper cleanup this issu is a histor one manifest in otelgin but potenti affect virtual all http relat middlewar refer for this issu includ http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873e60b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"id\": \"d2762ef7a24b09d4\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.298903782411875, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1453233905883928, \"vector_similarity\": 0.65725803, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"873e60b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 8756, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:25\", \"token_count\": 2164, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- 2025-07-02T08:06:06Z · **cross-referenced** by dmathieu ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7541\\n\\n- 2025-07-02T15:30:57Z · **cross-referenced** by flc1125 ← https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455\\n\\n- 2025-11-03T09:18:09Z · **cross-referenced** by pellared ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648\\n\\n- 2026-01-16T17:41:03Z · **cross-referenced** by MrAlias ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/8419\\n\\n- 2026-04-21T06:02:25Z · **cross-referenced** by SAY-5 ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8851\\n\\n- 2026-05-31T02:40:32Z · **referenced** by SAY-5\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"2025 07 02t08 06 06z cross referenc by dmathieu http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7541 2025 07 02t15 30 57z cross referenc by flc1125 http github com golang go issu 74455 2025 11 03t09 18 09z cross referenc by pellar http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 2026 01 16t17 41 03z cross referenc by mralia http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8419 2026 04 21t06 02 25z cross referenc by say 5 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8851 2026 05 31t02 40 32z referenc by say 5\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"id\": \"a05a50342909f16e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2937871516911204, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11686568813017206, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7066039, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 16121, \"chunk_count\": 10, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 5002, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"the HTTP server holds the original request, and using otelgin.Middleware replaces the request with [c.request = c.request.WithContext(ctx)](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/blob/cb45b36c145ff13e4ba76fd9e02ef39297c906b5/instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gintrace.go#L79), causing subsequent c.FormFile reads to fall on the new request. As a result, the original request held by the HTTP server does not have the MultipartForm, preventing it from being destroyed.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-01]\\n\\n# Issue: Using otelgin.Middleware will cause temporary MultipartForm files not to be destroyed. (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#5946)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946  \\n\\n**Author**: zacklpx  \\n\\n**Created**: 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **Updated**: 2025-07-03T13:28:05Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelgin  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (11)\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-01-11T11:28:03Z\\n\\n@akats7 Is there any plan to address this issue? For reference, a similar problem was resolved in Echo with this fix: [Echo-contrib PR #90](https://github.com/labstack/echo-contrib/pull/90/files#diff-86bf6c8ade26d5c58be942ac6765d89c8855c8713ba9a4d61249e16e3fa9c0fc).  If you're busy, I'd be happy to help by creating a PR to address it. Let me know!  \\n\\n---\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-01-12T13:54:25Z\\n\\ncc @akats7 as code owner.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-01-13T02:11:01Z\\n\\nHi @Yiling-J,\\n\\nFeel free to open a PR, I'll gladly review\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-07-02T08:35:01Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"the http server hold the origin request and use otelgin middlewar replac the request with c request c request withcontext ctx http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib blob cb45b36c145ff13e4ba76fd9e02ef39297c906b5 instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gintrac go l79 caus subsequ c formfil read to fall on the new request a a result the origin request held by the http server doe not have the multipartform prevent it from be destroy sourc id src issu 01 issu use otelgin middlewar will caus temporari multipartform file not to be destroy open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 5946 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 author zacklpx creat 2024 07 25t03 50 39z updat 2025 07 03t13 28 05z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open label bug area instrument instrument otelgin mileston discuss 11 yile j 2025 01 11t11 28 03z akats7 is there ani plan to address this issu for refer a similar problem wa resolv in echo with this fix echo contrib pr 90 http github com labstack echo contrib pull 90 file diff 86bf6c8ade26d5c58be942ac6765d89c8855c8713ba9a4d61249e16e3fa9c0fc if you re busi i d be happi to help by creat a pr to address it let me know dmathieu 2025 01 12t13 54 25z cc akats7 a code owner akats7 2025 01 13t02 11 01z hi yile j feel free to open a pr i ll glad review flc1125 2025 07 02t08 35 01z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"id\": \"35baa43d7c471818\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2894625016911204, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11686568813017206, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6921884, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 16121, \"chunk_count\": 10, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 5002, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T04:43:31Z\\n\\nJust found an open 2 year old issue this would fix #4588 \\n\\n---\\n\\n**nicksherron** — 2025-10-14T04:56:41Z\\n\\nThanks for the quick response @flc1125 , but I would like to offer a rebuttal. \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## This PR Fixes an Existing Bug, Not Introducing New Safety Mechanisms\\n\\nI respectfully disagree with the characterization that this PR \\\"introduces mechanisms for concurrency safety.\\\" The opposite is true: this PR removes problematic code that causes a data race.\\n\\nThe current code has a real, reproducible race condition reported in issue #4588 (open for 2 years). The race detector fails consistently. This is not theoretical—it violates Go's memory model.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"nicksherron 2025 10 14t04 43 31z just found an open 2 year old issu this would fix 4588 nicksherron 2025 10 14t04 56 41z thank for the quick respons flc1125 but i would like to offer a rebutt sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston this pr fix an exist bug not introduc new safeti mechan i respect disagre with the character that this pr introduc mechan for concurr safeti the opposit is true this pr remov problemat code that caus a data race the current code ha a real reproduc race condit report in issu 4588 open for 2 year the race detector fail consist this is not theoret it violat go s memori model sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"79dd2c776e5b2e7f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28329125269112043, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11686568813017206, \"vector_similarity\": 0.67161757, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"```\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T08:21:31Z\\n\\nWouldn't we be fixing this rather more easily with the following:\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n\\t\\tc.Request = c.Request.Clone(ctx)\\n\\n```\\n\\n[WithContext](https://pkg.go.dev/net/http#Request.WithContext) performs a shallow clone, and therefore doesn't clone the multipart form.\\n\\nHowever, [Clone](https://pkg.go.dev/net/http#Request.Clone) performs a deep copy, and makes an explicit clone of [MultipartForm](https://cs.opensource.google/go/go/+/refs/tags/go1.23.4:src/net/http/request.go;l=406).\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T14:39:53Z\\n\\nThe problem here is, go http request will call MultipartForm.RemoveAll() automatically when request finishes. However, the otelgin middleware creates a new request, and temporary files will be stored in this new request's MultipartForm field. Unfortunately, no one is calling MultipartForm.RemoveAll() on this new request.\\n\\nA deep clone wouldn’t resolve the problem because the MultipartForm is also copied. A shallow clone might seem like it should work since the MultipartForm field is shared, but it doesn’t. This is because the MultipartForm field is lazily initialized—it’s only assigned a value when you [parse the form](https://github.com/golang/go/blob/6da16013ba4444e0d71540f68279f0283a92d05d/src/net/http/request.go#L1403). As a result, in the middleware, the field is nil.\\n\\nRelated issues: https://github.com/golang/go/issues/58809, https://github.com/labstack/echo/issues/2413\\n\\nI think other OpenTelemetry middlewares, such as otelmux and otelehco, might also have the same issue.\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T14:55:45Z\\n\\nWhat if we parse the form before making the new request?\\n\\nWouldn't we share the object then?\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T15:31:10Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t08 21 31z wouldn t we be fix this rather more easili with the follow suggest c request c request clone ctx withcontext http pkg go dev net http request withcontext perform a shallow clone and therefor doesn t clone the multipart form howev clone http pkg go dev net http request clone perform a deep copi and make an explicit clone of multipartform http c opensourc googl go go ref tag go1 23 4 src net http request go l 406 yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t14 39 53z the problem here is go http request will call multipartform removeal automat when request finish howev the otelgin middlewar creat a new request and temporari file will be store in this new request s multipartform field unfortun no one is call multipartform removeal on this new request a deep clone wouldn t resolv the problem becaus the multipartform is also copi a shallow clone might seem like it should work sinc the multipartform field is share but it doesn t this is becaus the multipartform field is lazili initi it s onli assign a valu when you pars the form http github com golang go blob 6da16013ba4444e0d71540f68279f0283a92d05d src net http request go l1403 a a result in the middlewar the field is nil relat issu http github com golang go issu 58809 http github com labstack echo issu 2413 i think other opentelemetri middlewar such a otelmux and otelehco might also have the same issu dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t14 55 45z what if we pars the form befor make the new request wouldn t we share the object then yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t15 31 10z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"0b66ff59ca7469a0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2806708546085338, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11534824944076258, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6664236, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- 2025-12-04T23:38:10Z · **closed** by MrAlias\\n\\n- 2026-04-03T11:34:34Z · **milestoned** by pellared → untracked\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"2025 12 04t23 38 10z close by mralia 2026 04 03t11 34 34z mileston by pellar untrack\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874bc7c88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"id\": \"aa358b18acc3fae2\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27573726909721336, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.06554727013887625, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7661806, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874bc7c88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8059.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 2849, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 1120, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"issue 5946 July 2025 marked duplicate dmathieu duplicate of what related issue 4588 status\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The work is **not merged or complete** in the dataset.\n\n- PR [#6609](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609) remains **open** (last updated 2025-11-13), with a +95/−0 proposed `otelgin` change and tests. It implements cleanup via `MultipartForm.RemoveAll()` after middleware processing. [SRC-PR-01](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609)\n- The key unresolved concern is compatibility: cleanup deletes the temporary files before an outer/upstream middleware returning later can read them. The PR gained tests demonstrating that behavior, but reviewers were still seeking agreement that it is the intended contract. A reattach-the-form alternative and prototype PR #8161 were raised; maintainers questioned whether that alternative fixes the underlying cloned-request cleanup problem. [SRC-PR-01](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609)\n- The Go SIG had recommended that middleware clean up temporary resources, and the discussion favored keeping this PR narrowly scoped to `otelgin`; similar risks may exist in other HTTP middleware. [SRC-PR-01](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609), [SRC-NOTE-04](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479584781)\n- Issue [#5946](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946) is recorded as **open** in the dataset, though its timeline also says it was marked as a duplicate on 2025-07-02. It remains cross-referenced to #6609. [SRC-ISSUE-01](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946)\n\nSo: there is an implemented, actively reviewed cleanup patch, but it is stalled pending final agreement on the `RemoveAll` behavior and has not landed."}}
